---
// How the migration fits together, drawn on the wall: today on the left, after the
// switch on the right, one middleware contract in between. Portrait so it reads on a phone.
---

<figure class="map">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 360 590" role="img" aria-labelledby="map-title map-desc">
    <title id="map-title">How the migration fits together</title>
    <desc id="map-desc">
      Today, the Shopware webshop sends orders through the middleware's old adapter to the legacy back
      office. After the switch, the Shopify webshop sends orders through the new adapter to Odoo. Both
      adapters sit behind one middleware contract. The hard part is the switch-over: moving every order
      from the old side to the new side while the shop keeps running.
    </desc>

    <text class="col" x="95" y="22" text-anchor="middle">Today</text>
    <text class="col" x="265" y="22" text-anchor="middle">After the switch</text>
    <path class="divider" d="M180 34 V140 M180 316 V420" />

    <g class="card">
      <rect x="20" y="36" width="150" height="64" />
      <text class="t" x="34" y="62">Shopware</text>
      <text class="s" x="34" y="82">old webshop</text>
    </g>
    <g class="card">
      <rect x="190" y="36" width="150" height="64" />
      <text class="t" x="204" y="62">Shopify</text>
      <text class="s" x="204" y="82">new webshop</text>
    </g>

    <path class="wire" d="M95 104 V146 M88 138 L95 147 L102 138" />
    <path class="wire" d="M265 104 V146 M258 138 L265 147 L272 138" />
    <text class="lbl" x="102" y="128">orders</text>
    <text class="lbl" x="272" y="128">orders</text>

    <g class="hub">
      <rect x="20" y="152" width="320" height="150" />
      <text class="t" x="36" y="180">Middleware</text>
      <text class="s" x="36" y="199">one contract for both sides</text>
      <g class="chip">
        <rect x="36" y="216" width="138" height="66" />
        <text class="t sm" x="48" y="240">old adapter</text>
        <text class="s" x="48" y="260">runs today’s shop</text>
      </g>
      <g class="chip">
        <rect x="186" y="216" width="138" height="66" />
        <text class="t sm" x="198" y="240">new adapter</text>
        <text class="s" x="198" y="260">fetch, sync, retry</text>
      </g>
    </g>

    <path class="wire" d="M105 306 V348 M98 340 L105 349 L112 340" />
    <path class="wire" d="M255 306 V348 M248 340 L255 349 L262 340" />
    <text class="lbl" x="97" y="330" text-anchor="end">sale orders</text>
    <text class="lbl" x="262" y="330">sale orders</text>

    <g class="card">
      <rect x="20" y="354" width="150" height="64" />
      <text class="t" x="34" y="380">Back office</text>
      <text class="s" x="34" y="400">legacy system</text>
    </g>
    <g class="card">
      <rect x="190" y="354" width="150" height="64" />
      <text class="t" x="204" y="380">Odoo</text>
      <text class="s" x="204" y="400">new ERP</text>
    </g>

    <g class="hot" transform="rotate(-2 180 510)">
      <rect x="56" y="462" width="248" height="96" />
      <text class="t" x="72" y="490">The switch-over</text>
      <text class="s ink" x="72" y="512">Move from left to right while</text>
      <text class="s ink" x="72" y="530">the shop keeps running.</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>How it fits together. Left: today. Right: after the switch.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .map {
    margin: 0;
  }

  svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    overflow: visible;
    font-family: var(--font);
  }

  .col {
    font-size: var(--fs-label);
    font-weight: 700;
    fill: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .divider {
    stroke: var(--ink-2);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-dasharray: 4 5;
    fill: none;
  }

  .card rect,
  .chip rect {
    fill: #fff;
  }

  .card rect {
    filter: drop-shadow(0 8px 9px rgb(22 23 26 / 0.22));
  }

  .hub > rect {
    fill: var(--blue);
    filter: drop-shadow(0 10px 12px rgb(22 23 26 / 0.25));
  }

  .hot rect {
    fill: var(--pink);
    filter: drop-shadow(0 10px 12px rgb(22 23 26 / 0.25));
  }

  .t {
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    font-weight: 800;
    fill: var(--ink);
  }

  .t.sm {
    font-size: var(--fs-small);
  }

  .s {
    font-size: var(--fs-label);
    font-weight: 500;
    fill: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .hub > .s,
  .s.ink {
    fill: var(--ink);
  }

  .lbl {
    font-size: var(--fs-label);
    font-weight: 600;
    fill: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .wire {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--ink);
    stroke-width: 3;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: var(--fs-small);
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
</style>
